WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.520
To activate its effect, I send Destiny 
HERO — Dynatag to my graveyard!

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:09.040
When my life is lower than yours,

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:14.190
I can negate battle damage, and deal 
1000 damage to both players!

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:14.930
What?

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.620
Hurry!

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.140
Commander, are you injured?!

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.780
Commander?

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:36.310
The Aquaria Project.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:42.090
In their plan to create an ideal world, 
the Fusion Dimension's Academia

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:47.420
has driven Heartland City, in the Xyz 
Dimension, to the brink of obliteration.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:25.990
The Bonds of Resistance

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:37.960
Commander?

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.410
There... Over there.

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:44.040
That's where I saw Kaito!

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.520
Kaito...

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.380
Let's go.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.070
What are you doing?

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.460
You want to bring him back, don't you?

00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:00.830
I attack with my three Galaxy-Eyes 
Cipher Dragons!

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.660
Kaito! We've been searching for you...

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:08.970
Don't get in my way!

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:13.080
I told you that I already severed ties to you.

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:16.540
Kaito...

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:20.580
W-Wait! Please spare us!

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.280
Are you ready to make your confessions?

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:34.090
Wait... Hey!

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:36.860
Stop being stubborn and come back.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.500
Don't you realize how worried Sayaka is?

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:40.770
Kaito!

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:45.720
Syun...

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:52.770
Get in my way, and I'll turn you into a card!

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.480
You can try it... with a duel!

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.690
Field Spell Crossover.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:08.010
Wait a minute!

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.170
Hey! What are you thinking?

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:11.360
We're on the same side.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.950
Guess we'll just have to see how it goes.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:20.270
Duel!

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.480
I'll take the first turn.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:26.870
I summon Raidraptor — Vanishing 
Lanius from my hand!

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:33.200
The turn I successfully summon it,

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:38.270
I can Special Summon another Vanishing 
Lanius from my hand.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:41.040
And Retrofit Lanius is

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:45.580
treated as a Raid Raptor 
currently on the field.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:51.690
I Special Summon Retrofit Lanius 
as a Vanishing Lanius!

00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:02.710
One Retrofit Lanius can also count 
as two Xyz components.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:07.660
I Overlay Vanishing Lanius and Retrofit Lanius!

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:15.460
Hidden falcon, raise your sharpened 
claws from adversity

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.330
and show your wings of rebellion!

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:19.230
Xyz Summon!

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:24.950
Appear, Rank 4 Raidraptor — Rise Falcon!

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:31.240
You took the first turn to show 
off that disgrace?

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:34.800
Rise Falcon's effect

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:39.420
activates if the opponent has a Special 
Summoned monster on their field.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:44.060
But I have no monsters, and you can't attack.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:47.360
Summoning it now is merely wasted effort.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:50.000
Try me, then...

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.930
I activate my Continuous Spell 
Raptor's Intercept Formation!

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:57.250
It means that, once per opponent's turn,

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:01.070
if an Xyz Summoned Raid Raptor is attacked,

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:04.940
I can swap its attack and defense points 
during damage calculation!

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:09.600
When this happens, Rise Falcon's 
attack points will be 2000!

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:12.600
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:15.390
My turn!

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:18.570
When I have no monsters on 
my side of the field

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:23.090
and my opponent has a monster that's 
Special Summoned from his Extra Deck,

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:26.060
I can Special Summon this card from my hand.

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:30.620
Come, Cipher Twin Raptor!

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:37.710
Then, I Normal Summon Cipher Wing!

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:42.280
And by tributing this Cipher Wing,

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:46.080
I increase the level of Cipher 
monsters on the field by 4!

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:54.830
One Cipher Twin Raptor counts 
as two Xyz components.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:58.030
I Overlay with Cipher Twin Raptor!

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.970
Galaxy shining in the darkness...

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:08.610
Dwell within the god of vengeance 
and become my servant!

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.070
Xyz Summon!

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:16.250
Descend, Rank 8 Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon!

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:19.560
Although his Continuous Spell

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:24.210
raised his monster's attack points 
to 2000, he can't fight that.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:29.530
And Galaxy-Eyes has the Cipher 
Projection that beat us.

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:33.730
I activate Galaxy-Eyes's monster effect.

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:36.070
I use one Overlay Unit

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:40.420
to take control of a monster on your side 
of the field, with its effect negated,

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:41.670
until the end of my turn.

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:43.700
Cipher Projection!

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:52.330
I activate Continuous Spell Raptor's 
Intercept Formation's other effect!

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:56.930
Once, during each of our turns, 
I can negate a card effect

00:07:56.930 --> 00:07:59.030
targeting a Raid Raptor.

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:01.570
In that case, battle!

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:04.800
I attack Rise Falcon with Cipher Dragon!

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:08.140
Annihilating Cipher Stream!

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:11.370
During damage calculation,

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:16.170
my Continuous Spell's effect lets me 
exchange attack and defense points.

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:17.710
It isn't enough...

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:19.140
He's gonna get beaten.

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:23.870
Action Spell Miracle!

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:27.320
I negate destruction by battle, 
halving damage taken.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.790
The instant damage calculation ends,

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:36.900
Rise Falcon's attack points return to normal.

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:39.420
Action Spell?

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:42.810
We use Action Cards on 
the field to help us fight.

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:45.200
That's how we Lancers do things.

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:49.410
You use Action Cards, too?

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:55.970
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:59.850
Did you intend to use that Action 
Card thing from the start?

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:01.550
What are you trying to say?

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.760
You've become a coward.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:06.650
You can say that once more, after you win.

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:08.730
My turn!

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:14.170
I activate Rank-Up-Magic Raid Force!

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.970
Using Rise Falcon as a component,

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:20.870
I Xyz Summon a Raid Raptor 
of one rank higher.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:23.230
Rank-Up Xyz Change!

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:27.750
Appear, Rank 5 Raid Raptor — Blaze Falcon!

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:30.820
I activate Blaze Falcon's effect!

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:33.420
I use one Overlay Unit

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:37.440
to destroy all monsters Special 
Summoned to your side of the field,

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:40.330
and for each, I deal 500 damage to you.

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:43.480
I activate my trap Cipher Bit!

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:47.440
I negate a Cipher monster's destruction,

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.770
and this card becomes an Overlay Unit.

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:55.210
What?

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:57.480
Not only did he negate the destruction,

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:00.580
he also turned a trap card into an Overlay Unit?

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.620
Amazing...

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.140
When did he become able to do that?

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:09.050
While he's been off fighting by himself, 
he's also been polishing his skills?

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:12.020
Alone?

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:16.730
But Blaze Falcon can attack you directly.

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:23.270
Is that...

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:26.010
It's coming from the Resistance base.

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:27.870
You don't think... Academia...

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:35.050
Then, when Blaze Falcon deals battle damage,

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:37.820
I destroy one monster on your side of the field!

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:46.990
I understand the pain of losing your family.

00:10:46.990 --> 00:10:49.130
When I learned Ruri had been taken,

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:52.330
I wanted to destroy Academia on my own, too.

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:54.780
What could you understand?

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:58.270
I activate my trap Cipher Spectrum!

00:10:58.270 --> 00:11:01.570
When a Cipher monster with 
Overlay Units is destroyed,

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:05.540
I can Special Summon that Cipher 
monster from my graveyard!

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:09.950
And I Special Summon another monster, 
of the same kind, from my Extra Deck!

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.890
I now end my turn.

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:21.590
I thought he'd beaten it. 
But now, there are two more...

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:26.190
Even if you're defeated, inch your 
way up and stand with your allies.

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:28.300
That is the soul of the Resistance.

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:31.770
You haven't forgotten those old feelings.

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:37.940
With your allies...

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:46.920
Stop it! Both of you!

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.360
Yuya?

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:49.390
He's...

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:52.540
Kurosaki! Kaito!

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:54.360
Why are you fighting your allies?

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:56.330
None of your business. Get lost.

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:58.030
Allen...

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:00.090
You call us allies?

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:03.710
Galaxy-Eyes is an extension of myself.

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:06.970
It isn't a trivial "ally"!

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:09.960
I am the only one on my side now!

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:11.940
My turn!

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:13.340
Yuya...

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:17.880
Yuya, we have to let Syun 
handle this for now.

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:22.620
Battle! Cipher Dragon attacks Blaze Falcon!

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:25.480
Annihilating Cipher Stream!

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:28.240
The effect of Raptor's Intercept Formation

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:33.430
switches Blaze Falcon's attack and defense 
points during battle calculation!

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:37.640
And I activate my Continuous 
Trap Overlay Armor!

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:42.400
I use one Overlay Unit on Blaze Falcon

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.540
to prevent its destruction!

00:12:49.060 --> 00:12:51.080
When damage calculation ends,

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:54.290
Blaze Falcon's attack points return to normal.

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:56.920
That was a close one...

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:58.760
Hang in there, Kurosaki.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:07.700
When I went to the Standard Dimension 
without telling anyone,

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:10.320
Ute came after me.

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:14.390
Because I had an ally named Ute, 
I'm standing here right now.

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:16.730
Syun...

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:19.180
I thought I told you to be quiet.

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:27.290
With my other Cipher Dragon, 
I attack Blaze Falcon again!

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:29.790
Annihilating Cipher Stream!

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:32.120
The effect of Overlay Armor

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:37.860
uses Blaze Falcon's other Overlay Unit 
to prevent destruction once more.

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:39.830
But you still take damage.

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:43.640
Kurosaki!

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:53.130
I set one card and end my turn.

00:13:56.580 --> 00:14:01.550
Blaze Falcon remains, but its 
wings have been clipped.

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:04.460
Blaze Falcon's attack points are 1000.

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:07.610
It's used all its Overlay Units, too.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:10.920
Nothing in his hand, and only 500 life left.

00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:12.530
What's he gonna do?

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:22.970
Even if you drive me to the brink 
of despair, I won't yield.

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:27.180
I'm fighting not only for myself. But for you, too.

00:14:27.520 --> 00:14:30.880
So after being driven this far, 
you still won't give up?!

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:32.510
I won't!

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:34.350
Not until I persuade you...

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:36.760
I've never seen Syun like this.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:42.860
Syun is trying to use this duel 
to make Kaito listen.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:46.300
My duel with you really begins now.

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:50.200
I'll make you understand the path 
you should truly be walking!

00:14:52.190 --> 00:14:53.610
My turn!

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:56.380
Another Action Card?

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:59.630
What could someone like you, who relies on

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:02.310
the power of strangers, make me understand?!

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:05.200
Not strangers! Allies!

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:07.900
Action Cards are the power of my allies!

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:09.720
The power of allies?

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:12.420
I will fight, believing in my allies.

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:19.100
Battle... I attack Cipher Dragon 
with Blaze Falcon!

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:20.670
You're being too reckless, Syun!

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:23.570
Cipher Dragon has 3000 attack points.

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:26.970
I'll reach him!

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:29.570
I have allies besides Ute!

00:15:34.360 --> 00:15:37.000
Action Spell Attack Force!

00:15:37.420 --> 00:15:38.810
During battle,

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:44.690
it raises the attack points of 
the weaker monster by 600!

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:51.800
In the Synchro Dimension, I forged 
strong bonds with new allies, also.

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:55.500
Action Spell High Dive!

00:15:57.200 --> 00:16:02.660
Until the end of the turn, it increases one 
monster's attack points by 1000!

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:07.810
I found allies in various dimensions.

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:11.850
By meeting them, I learned 
the importance of allies!

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:13.400
Allies?

00:16:21.510 --> 00:16:22.590
Sayaka...

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:25.030
He did it!

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:26.930
What?

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:35.570
Looks like it didn't reach me.

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:41.980
That's the Action Spell Take Flight.

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:46.520
Take Flight can only be used when 
an opponent is attacking.

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:48.820
Damn, so that's why...

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:52.110
"Action Cards are the power of my allies."

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:54.000
That's what you said.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:58.300
But your reliance on them has 
caused you to lose your wings.

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:02.970
When you lose allies you trust,

00:17:02.970 --> 00:17:06.240
people become captive to unspeakable sorrow.

00:17:06.740 --> 00:17:08.940
They're nothing but chains that hobble you!

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:14.160
Because I don't want to lose 
my allies, I fight with them!

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:16.420
Carrying the burden of those I've lost.

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:21.750
I activate my Quick-Play Spell Rank-Up-Magic 
Doom Double Force!

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:26.720
I can Special Summon an Xyz 
Monster destroyed by battle,

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:33.690
and use it as a component, to Xyz Summon 
a Raid Raptor of twice the rank!

00:17:37.670 --> 00:17:40.360
Ultimate falcon,

00:17:40.360 --> 00:17:45.110
inherit the will of your many colleagues, 
and fly to the sky of victory!

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:47.810
Rank-Up Xyz Change!

00:17:47.810 --> 00:17:52.660
Appear, Level 10 Raidraptor — 
Ultimate Falcon!

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:56.750
It has more attack points 
than Cipher Dragon.

00:17:57.080 --> 00:18:00.860
And I activate my trap Ultimate Full Burst!

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:06.960
It allows the effects of Ranked-Up Xyz 
Monsters that require Overlay Units

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:08.500
to be activated during battle.

00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:13.240
And that monster can attack all monsters 
on your side of the field!

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:18.040
I use one of Ultimate Falcon's Overlay Units

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:23.450
to negate all cards on your side of the field, 
reducing their attack points by 1000.

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:28.150
I attack the first Cipher Dragon 
with Ultimate Falcon!

00:18:28.510 --> 00:18:31.120
Final Glorious Bright!

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:37.390
Yes!

00:18:37.390 --> 00:18:39.300
The next attack will finish it!

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:42.480
This is the power of those who 
believe in their allies.

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:45.500
And, Kaito, you are one of those allies!

00:18:57.430 --> 00:18:59.930
I remember back in duel school...

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:03.070
Back then, when Kaito and Syun were dueling,

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:05.060
children would always gather around.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:10.230
The children would watch them, 
with admiration in their eyes.

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:14.420
How do you know that?

00:19:15.970 --> 00:19:18.170
Ute is inside me.

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:19.600
Ute?

00:19:19.600 --> 00:19:21.310
Inside you?

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:23.830
No, what are you talking about?

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:29.010
Then, he is near... I had a feeling.

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:36.570
This will finish it!

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:38.820
Go, Ultimate Falcon!

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:41.790
Final Glorious Bright!

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:50.700
I activate the effect of Cipher 
Mirror Knight in my hand!

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:53.820
By sending this card, and one card 
on my field, to the graveyard,

00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:59.690
I can Special Summon one Cipher Dragon 
sent to the graveyard by battle!

00:20:02.310 --> 00:20:06.520
The trap card I sent to the graveyard 
was Cipher Clone Magic.

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:12.090
Its effect lets me send Continuous Spell Cipher 
Interference from my deck to my graveyard,

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:13.880
to use its effect!

00:20:14.390 --> 00:20:18.720
When there are two or more of the same 
Cipher monster on my side of the field,

00:20:18.720 --> 00:20:23.460
one of them has its attack points 
doubled until battle ends.

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:31.580
Ultimate Full Burst's effect  means 
that you must attack all monsters.

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:35.340
Even Cipher Dragon, who has 
more attack points.

00:20:48.460 --> 00:20:50.090
K-Kurosaki...

00:20:50.090 --> 00:20:51.430
N-No.

00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:58.370
Are you ready to make your confession?

00:21:02.310 --> 00:21:03.240
Hey, sto—

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:04.210
Stop!

00:21:07.860 --> 00:21:10.880
Please... Spare Syun.

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:12.380
If we lose Syun, too...

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:14.910
And after Ruri...

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:18.360
You're wrong, Sayaka! 
That wasn't your fault!

00:21:18.700 --> 00:21:20.820
No, it was my fault!

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:28.170
If we duel and I win, you must do as I say.

00:21:28.170 --> 00:21:29.770
All right?

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:38.410
Back then, because I couldn't be brave,

00:21:39.140 --> 00:21:41.110
Ruri was taken away!

00:22:05.350 --> 00:22:06.470
Kaito...

00:23:50.370 --> 00:23:53.130
The Academia students are fighting

00:23:53.130 --> 00:23:56.810
for a plan that will let all people live in peace.

00:23:56.810 --> 00:23:58.240
A plan?

00:23:58.240 --> 00:24:03.490
The Professor plans to unite dimensions, 
to create an ideal world for everyone.

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:05.690
But in actuality,

00:24:05.690 --> 00:24:09.830
it's a plan for Academia to invade 
and take over all the dimensions.

00:24:10.530 --> 00:24:14.570
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Aquaria Project.

00:24:14.570 --> 00:24:16.650
The fun is only getting started!
